
What is LambdaExpression?
 - Lambda Expression id Anonymous Function.
     - No Name, No Modifier, No Return Type

Benefits of Lambda.
  - Reduce Line of code.
  - Sequential and Parallel execution support by passing behavior as an argument in method.
  - To call APIs very effectively.
  - To write a more Readable,Maintainable and Concise code.

Rules of Lambda
  - If The body of the lambda Expression contains only one statement then curly braces are optional.
  - java compiler also inter the type of passed in arguments, hence type is optional.

Functional Interface:
   - If the importance contains only one abstract methods then it is functional interface.(eg. Runnable, callable, Comparable)
   - To call lambda we required functional interface.
   - lambda is used to implement functional interface is simple and sloat manner.


